                                                  \setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
                                                  \begin{document}$$\begin{array}{llllllr}\Delta {{\rm{x}}}&=&f(\Delta {{\rm{evp}}}\cdot {s}_{{{\rm{x}}},{{\rm{evp}}}},\Delta {{{\rm{alb}}}}_{{{\rm{srf}}}}\cdot {s}_{{{\rm{x}}},{{\rm{alb}}}})&&&&,{{\rm{with}}}\\ {s}_{{{\rm{x}}},{{\rm{evp}}}}&=&\frac{\Delta {{\rm{x}}}}{\Delta {{{\rm{alb}}}}_{{{\rm{TOA}}}}}\cdot f\left(\frac{\Delta {{\rm{cld}}}}{\Delta {{\rm{evp}}}}\right)\hfill&&&&,{{\rm{and}}}\\ {s}_{{{\rm{x}}},{{\rm{alb}}}}&=&\frac{\Delta {{\rm{x}}}}{\Delta {{{\rm{alb}}}}_{{{\rm{TOA}}}}}\cdot f\left({{\rm{cld}}},\frac{\Delta {{\rm{cld}}}}{\Delta {{{\rm{alb}}}}_{{{\rm{srf}}}}}\right).\hfill&&&&\end{array}$$\end{document}Δx=f(Δevp⋅sx,evp,Δalbsrf⋅sx,alb),withsx,evp=ΔxΔalbTOA⋅fΔcldΔevp,andsx,alb=ΔxΔalbTOA⋅fcld,ΔcldΔalbsrf.

Furthermore, our results suggest, that synergistic effects are negligible in the relation of surface albedo, evapotranspiration and top-of-atmosphere shortwave radiation, so that the overall response should simply be the sum of the responses to albedo- and evapotranspiration changes: 4\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
