Our results also suggest that non-local effects are largely independent of the type of perturbation and mainly arise due to change in the meridional heat transport. Thus, the non-local effects should be roughly proportional to the magnitude of the local temperature response and, therefore to the local changes in evapotranspiration (Δevplocal) and surface albedo (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
