There is substantial spatial variability in the low-altitude cloud cover and the sensitivities, sx,evp, sx,alb, are, therefore, highly dependent on the latitudinal band (lat) in which the land surface change occurs. It is conceivable to deduce them based on the local climate conditions and known relations, such as the Clausius-Clapeyron equation. However, in the present investigation, we follow a different approach and determine the region-specific sensitivities (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
